From 4911066c502f20db212d1938f9f3edd89438b418 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 12:55:51 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(inventory): define Bedrock request and recipe codecs

Introduce the request, response, and recipe models with their versioned codecs before wiring inventory behavior. Keep enum mappings and codec tests with the protocol foundation so the later container patch starts from a typed Bedrock interface.

Retain the native TextProcessingEventOrigin mapping with unknown=-1. A capture from Bedrock 1.26.51.1 build 51061372, protocol 2193, confirms this sentinel in accepted merchant requests. The schema enum list does not describe its numeric starting value.

Retain all dynamic multi-recipe UUIDs and their server-assigned network IDs. Bedrock 1.26.51.1 build 51061372, protocol 2193, native cartography captures use these IDs for map cloning, extension, and locking through CraftRecipeOptional. Dropping this array prevents containers from resolving the recipes. Keep unknown UUIDs and unsigned IDs intact so decoding does not depend on a closed list of vanilla recipes.
